Hi Richard,

Here is the fitted model output for our top-ranked model on which
we're running the bootstrap:

Call:
distsamp(formula = ~temp ~ stock + stock2, data = umf, keyfun =
"halfnorm",
    output = "density", unitsOut = "ha")

Density:
            Estimate      SE      z  P(>|z|)
(Intercept) -3.02072 0.18445 -16.38 2.78e-60
stock        0.68021 0.48637   1.40 1.62e-01
stock2      -0.00597 0.00315  -1.89 5.84e-02

Detection:
                 Estimate    SE     z  P(>|z|)
sigma(Intercept)    4.568 0.282 16.20 4.74e-59
sigmatemp          -0.475 0.155 -3.06 2.23e-03

AIC: 649.7065

I have re-run parboot, even with fewer simulations, but we got the
same error.  I ran simulate(temp_stock2) multiple times and that all
looks reasonable.
Yes, we standardized our covariates before running any models, and
unfortunately I don't know what you mean when you ask if any of the
parameter estimates are near a boundary...

Thanks for the assistance!

Sarah

